# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# Environment — never commit real credentials.
# .env.example IS tracked; it is the same file with the credentials blanked.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example

# Vendored wheels for non-PyPI dependencies (yukta). Binaries stay out of the
# repo — rebuild with scripts/build-yukta-wheel.sh; see backend/vendor/README.md,
# which is tracked so a fresh clone knows to run it.
backend/vendor/*.whl
backend/vendor/*.tar.gz

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
*.log

# Any mode's per-session uploads and generated pipeline artifacts
backend/modes/*/sessions/
backend/modes/*/pipeline/output/
backend/modes/*/pipeline/sessions/

# TB-v2 writes its run artifacts one level HIGHER than the patterns above —
# backend/modes/sessions/<session-id>/ and backend/modes/output/ — which
# `backend/modes/*/sessions/` does not match. These hold real trial-balance
# data for named entities (canonical_tb.parquet, fsli_summary, layer1_*), so
# leaving them unignored would push client financial data to a public remote.
backend/modes/sessions/
backend/modes/output/

# Generated by `python -m scripts.audit_fs_entities --json` — a corpus dump of
# every entity and its filing coverage. A diagnostic report, not source; nothing
# in the app reads it.
backend/fs_entities.json

FIN_LLM/

# A separately-cloned copy of the docling library's own repo, left sitting in
# this project's folder (it has its own .git, .claude, .codex dirs). Nothing
# in this codebase imports from it -- the real dependency is the pip-installed
# `docling-slim` package in ingestion/requirements.txt. Not this project's to
# push, and at 500MB+ it doesn't belong in this repo regardless.
docling/

# An older backup of .env, made before the ingestion feature was added.
# Same class of file as .env itself above -- real credentials, never committed.
.env.bak-before-ingest

# Loose files that ended up in this folder but are not this project's:
# an unrelated project's zipped-up working copy (contains ITS OWN .env with
# real credentials -- checked before excluding, not guessed), a stray IDE
# project file left over from the parent workspace, and a large reference PDF
# that was never deliberately checked in.
research_agent_tested.zip
*.iml
FS_AI_Audit_Final_Detailed_Team_Edition v4.0.pdf

# The local sample corpus the ingestion accuracy harness and manual upload
# testing read from (`tests/accuracy/cases/*.yaml` point `pdf:` paths into
# this directory, and `runner.py`'s `DATA` constant resolves them there) —
# real scanned financial statements for named entities. Same reasoning as
# `backend/modes/sessions/` above: this is client data, not source, and does
# not belong in a shared/public remote. A contributor who needs the corpus to
# run the accuracy harness fetches it out of band and places it here; without
# it, the harness fails open (`FileNotFoundError` on the missing PDF) rather
# than silently reporting a false pass.
data/
data.zip

# yukta's per-agent auto-save (AgentConfig.auto_save_chat=True, on by default
# in every SAR/Financial-Statement/Trial-Balance agent factory) — written
# relative to the process's cwd, so it can land at the repo root, under a
# mode's own directory, or both, depending on where the backend was started
# from. These hold real extracted report content from whatever entity was
# last processed, not source — confirmed accumulating here from a live SAR
# pipeline test run (see backend/modes/statutory_auditor_report/sar_prod_v3/
# GAP_CLOSURE_LOG.md, Phase 5) and would otherwise get committed by a plain
# `git add -A` without anyone noticing.
agent_chats/
chats/
